Track 2: "Who Carried the Larva Down?"
- Story & Context: Recorded in an abandoned hyperbaric testing tank in Falmouth, this confession piece was birthed when Elowen discovered a desiccated moth trapped inside the soundboard of her 1912 cello immediately following the news that her long-distance partner had severed ties from across the Atlantic. The track unfurls around her grief-stricken solo bowing, punctuated by Sean's brittle, skipping rimshots and an aching question whispered through an old diver’s intercom system. In an impulsive moment of catharsis during the final take, she ran her bow across the lowest C-string until the gut snapped against the fingerboard with a violent crack, leaving behind the haunting vocal take: "you left three thousand miles of silence on my wire."
