Track 3: Comb Filtering the Winter Swarm
- Story & Context: Local myth claims that months after the maintenance vessels abandoned the Bude shoreline, harbor hydrophones recorded anomalous melodic echoes sweeping through the bay that perfectly harmonized with Sean’s looped cello delays left bouncing through the dormant optic cables. Sitting in the cliffside lookout during a sleet storm, watching gannets dive into freezing breakers while the smell of woodsmoke drifted from the village, the trio stitched the lingering cable hum into a bittersweet, nine-minute farewell track. The composition closes the record on an unresolved open fifth, celebrating the eternal drift of sound between continents with the haunting vocoder line: "the swarm remembers every note we buried."
